Each answer is committed as sha256(salt || canonical JSON of {id, label, type}) with a 32-byte salt; the root is sha256 of the commitments joined by newlines in id order. At opening, check_open.py recomputes every commitment and the root from the answers.

**The SHA-256 of this document is anchored to the JIDEC ledger and stamped to Bitcoin. After anchoring, this record cannot be altered. Corrections are later entries that cite this one.**
